in ms. Reg.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 25 Ms. Reg. cum edd. Bad. et Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in exultatione.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 26 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini nostri Jesu.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 27 Latinius legendum putat  <HI REND="ITALIC">locorum.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 28 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de cella nostra.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 29 Ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">testem.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 30 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">accipias.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 31 Mss. codices Reg. et Vien. cum edd. Bad., Grav.
et Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">impendi ordinare digneris.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0422"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0422"><HEAD COM="0422">IN EPIST. VI ET VII.</HEAD> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 1 Mss. duo Big.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">amici,</HI>  non male.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 2 Mss duo Big.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0422"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0422"><HEAD COM="0422">IN EPIST. VIII.</HEAD> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 1 Expunximus vocem  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper,</HI>  quam addebat editio
Rosw. contra fidem aliorum codicum.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 2 Ita mss. duo Big. Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">supra.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 3 Ostendit summam miseriam ambitiosorum qui
emunt ancillas, id est, donis ambiunt gratiam feminarum
vilium, quae ipsis dominentur. SACCHIN. S. J.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 4 Sacchin. fortasse  <HI REND="ITALIC">decori.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 5 Ita mss. Bigotiani codices duo, Vaticani 4, et
ed. Bened. Ante erat  <HI REND="ITALIC">ac simulacra.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 6 Sic edd. Bened. et Grav. Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">affundam.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0422"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0422"><HEAD COM="0422">IN EPIST. IX.</HEAD> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 1 Ita ms. Vien. Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sal terra vividum, referens.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 2 Mss. codices Reg. et Vien. cum editis tribus,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">adnuere.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 3 Sacchin. consequentius videtur  <HI REND="ITALIC">abstinemus.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 4 Ed. Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">via peccati.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0422"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0422"><HEAD COM="0422">IN EPIST. X.</HEAD> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 1 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quamquam.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 2 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de nostris.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 3 Ms. Reg. et edd. 4,  <HI REND="ITALIC">a tuo corde.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 4 Mss. Reg. et Vien.  <HI REND="ITALIC">adferens.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0422"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0422"><HEAD COM="0422">IN EPIST. XI.</HEAD> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 1 Ms. Reg. cum editis Bad., Grav., Grin. et Schot.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">jocunditatis.</HI>  Et sic ubique iidem codices.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 2 Mss. Reg. et Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adfertur.</HI>  Et sic alibi.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 3 Ita ms. Vien. Ceteri codices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec solum.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 4 Sic repositum ex ms. codice Viennensi. Alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sat
habeas.</HI>  Et mox ex eodem ms. codice,  <HI REND="ITALIC">eligis;</HI>  alias,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">eligas.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 5 Ita mss. Reg. et Vien. cum ed. Grin. Ceteri,  <HI REND="ITALIC">spiritualium.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 6 Ms. Vien. et ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adsumpsit.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 7 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">singulatim.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 8 Ms. Reg. cum editis quatuor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia unus.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 9 Abest a ms. Vaticano hoc nomen, nec sane est
necessarium. SACCHIN.</P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 10 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">viventem.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0422"></COL> 11 Ms. codex Regius cum editis Bad. Gray. et Schot.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hircum cum peremtione.</HI></P> <P COM="0422"><COL N="0423"></COL> 12 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ista tam brevi.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 13 Abest  <HI REND="ITALIC">te</HI>  a ms. Reg. et edd. Bad. et Grav.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 14 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">habeat si se.</HI>  Et mox idem ms.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">si totum
se Deo credat.</HI>  Alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">si totum de se,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 15 Ita mss. Reg. et Vien. Editi codices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">plena est
perfectio.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 16 Ms. Vatic.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">habemus.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 17 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nihil.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 18 Ed. Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deum.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0423"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0423"><HEAD COM="0423">IN EPIST. XII.</HEAD> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 1 Ms. Reg. et edd. Bad. et Grav.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed et metuo.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 2 Ed. Scoth.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ope.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 3 Ita mss. codices Vat., Vien. et edd. Grin. et
Rosw. Alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">exhausit.</HI>  SACCHIN.: Forte sic scripsit
autor  <HI REND="ITALIC">exclusit,</HI>  alludens ad Apostolum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ubi est gloriatio
tua? exclusa est.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 4 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dominum.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 5 Sic ms. codex Vien. Alii codd.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in qua.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 6 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad Deum.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 7 Ms. Vien. et ed. Grin. in marg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">altipetax.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 8 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deo.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 9 Ms. codex Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">prolongare.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 10 Ita mss. Reg. et Vien. et ed. Grin. Alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Exuperium.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 11 Sic repositum ex ms. codice Viennensi. Alias,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">dignamini.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0423"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0423"><HEAD COM="0423">IN EPIST. XIII.</HEAD> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 1 Ms. codex Regius cum editis Bad. et Grav.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Olimpi.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 2 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ni caros.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 3 Sacchin.: An addendum  <HI REND="ITALIC">animo, quam sensu?</HI>  
Cum enim comparetur sensus animi et corporis, non
videtur hic  <HI REND="ITALIC">sensus</HI>  accipi pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">animo,</HI>  tamen nihil mutarim.
Nam sensum pro mente aut virtute interiore
sentiendi accipi, cum in sacris Litteris, ut,  <HI REND="ITALIC">aperuit
illis sensum,</HI>  tum a sanctis Patribus, et maxime a Paulino
certum est, ut epist. ad Ausonium,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Defore, Secreta
ignitus penetrans coelestia sensus.</HI>  Et cum sensus
quid commune sit interiori et exteriori, melius
absolute tribuitur ei qui praecipuus est. Quin adeo
videtur hic Paulinus accipere pro quadam virtute
sentiendi praesentia. Ait ergo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si verum est, nos interiori
virtute potius quam oculis et auribus videre et
audire,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 4 Ita S. Paulinus n. 10. Vulgata cum S. Augustino
in Speculo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in mortuum.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 5 Sacchin. perfrigide: lege  <HI REND="ITALIC">justi.</HI>  Sensus est:
Tanta res est cura sepulcri ob memoriam resurrectionis,
ut Abraham qui omnia reliquerat,  <HI REND="ITALIC">solum tamen
agrum sepulcro emerit.</HI>  Quo fuit exemplo justis
comparandi sibi  <HI REND="ITALIC">aeternam possessionem, nec terram
avaritiae, sed quietis.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 6 Ms. codex Regius cum editis Bad., Grav. et
Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">conjunx.</HI>  Ita et alibi.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 7  <HI REND="ITALIC">Suscitat et desiderium:</HI>  sic cum ms. codice Regio
EDIT. Chiffl. Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">suscitat ei desiderium.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 8 Vulgata Lat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sapientiae.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 9 Ms. Reg. et edd. Bad., Grav., Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">venerabilis,
et non.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 10 Ms. reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">notum ipsi.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 11 Sacchin.: An  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui sequimur.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 12 Latin.: forte  <HI REND="ITALIC">pauperum.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 13 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">coartentur.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 14 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adtollebas.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 15 Particulam  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  addidimus ex ms. Vien. et edd.
Grin. et Chiffl.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 16 Ita omnes codices praeter Rosv. in quo  <HI REND="ITALIC">trigesimos.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 17 Ita emendatum ex ms. codice Vien. et ed. Chiffl.
Verissima lectio quam confirmant sequentia. In aliis
codicibus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">exceperant.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 18 Sic ms. Vien. et ed. Chiffl. Ante erat  <HI REND="ITALIC">vel exterioribus.</HI>  
Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de exterioribus.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 19 Particula  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  addit ex mss. codicibus Reg., Vien.,
et ed. Chiffl.</P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0423"></COL> 20 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum motus.</HI></P> <P COM="0423"><COL N="0424"></COL> 21 Ita ms. Reg. cum edd. tribus. Ed. Rosv.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Salomonem.</HI>  
Et sic ubique.</P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 22 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">muneraberis.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 23 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">gloriatur.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 24 Sic mss. Reg. Vien. et edd. Bad., Grav. Grin. et
Chiffl. Alii duo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et qui accepisti.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 25 Ms. Reg. cum edd. Bad. Grav. et Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui specialiter.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 26 Ms. Vatic.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vitalium.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 27 Ms. Reg. et edd. Bad. et Grav.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">centuplo,</HI>  ut infra
 <HI REND="ITALIC">duplo,</HI>  vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">triplo.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 28 Edd. Bad. et Grav.  <HI REND="ITALIC">civitate pietatem.</HI>  Latinius legendum
docet  <HI REND="ITALIC">pietate civitatem.</HI>  Vulgata lectio, quam
retinemus, optima et mss. ac tribus editis codicibus
consentanea et Floro Lugdunensi in Catena in epist.
Pauli lib. II. Vide praeterea n. 43.</P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 29 Addendum videtur  <HI REND="ITALIC">carnis</HI>  ex more autoris, quamvis
etiam in Vaticano absit. Eodem modo periodo
praecedenti deesse videtur aliquid tale,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sauciatus
corpore,</HI>  ut opponatur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed invulnerabilis corde.</HI>  SACCHIN.</P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 30 Ita ms. Reg., Florus in Catena, et ed. Chiffl.
Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">verum nec.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 31 Ed. Schot. et Chiffl.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui eumdem.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 32 Latinius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fissis.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 33 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">reddat.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 34 Ita mss. Reg., Vien. et Chiffl. Ceteri codices,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">cujusque.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 35 Sic ms. Vien. et ed. Chiffl. Alii codd.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">promisit.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 36  <HI REND="ITALIC">A mortuis, ostendit.</HI>  Expunximus particulam  <HI REND="ITALIC">et,</HI>  
quae aberat a ms. Vien. et edd. Schot. et Chiffl.</P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 37 Ms. Reg. et ed. Bad. et Grav.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">conjunx.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0424"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0424"><HEAD COM="0424">IN EPIST. XIV.</HEAD> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 1 Ed. Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vitae.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 2 Sic. mss. Vien. et Reg. Editi codices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">alterum.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 3 Ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">recipiantur.</HI></P></DIV1> <COL N="0424"></COL> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0424"><HEAD COM="0424">IN EPIST. XV.</HEAD> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 1 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia liberasti;</HI>  ms. Vatic.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qua liberas.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 2 Ita ms. Vien. Alii codices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">supra lectum.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 3 Ms. Reg. cum ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Basili.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 4 Ib. D  <HI REND="ITALIC">qua petitionem nostram in vestro.</HI>  ms. Reg.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qua qua,</HI>  etc. ms. Viennensis codex,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum qua petitionem
nostram vestro.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 5 Sic repositum ex ms. codice Viennensi. Ceteri,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">recipimus.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 6 Ms. Vien.  <HI REND="ITALIC">abhorruit.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 7 Ms. Vien.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domino.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 8 Ms. Reg.  <HI REND="ITALIC">testum.</HI></P> <P COM="0424"><COL N="0424"></COL> 9 Expunximus particulam  <HI REND="ITALIC">a</HI>  quae deerat in mss.
