 <HI REND="ITALIC">sed eorum.</HI>  Deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed</HI>  in editione Rosv.</P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 12 Ms. Reg. et edd. quatuor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dominicum verbum.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 13 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">reservandis.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 14 Ms. Reg. cum editis quatuor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed de peregrinis.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 15 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qua.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 16 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">terminasset, nec te falsi arguerem.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 17 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non tuleramus.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 18 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">animae nostrae visceribus;</HI>  nec male:
in epistola enim 23 ad Severum, n. 38,  <HI REND="ITALIC">tunc anima
nostra totis . . . visceribus accensa.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 19 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">accersit.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 20 Ms. Vat. et ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quo.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 21 Ita mss. codices. At editi,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nostra Deus.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 22 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut vis, meta . . . </HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 23 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">tunc vincit.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 24 Ms. codex Vaticanus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">transnatavit.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 25 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sacramentum.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 26 Deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">nostri</HI>  in ms. Vien.</P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0428"></COL> 27 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in illo.</HI></P> <P COM="0428"><COL N="0429"></COL> 28 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">deinde.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 29 Ms. Reg. et editi codices quatuor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quam Apostolus
docet, quam etiam,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 30 Ms. Reg. et editi codices Bad. et Grav.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod
nobis impendiore.</HI>  Ed. Grin.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod nobis impensiore.</HI>  
Ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae nobis impensiore.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 31 Ms. Vatic.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod peccato,</HI>  id est corpus, inquit
Sacchinus. Et mox idem ms. codex,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod peccatum
non fecit.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 32 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in lege peccati.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 33 Ms. Vat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">item dicit.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 34 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">incendat.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 35 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dignamque . . . frugem.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 36 Ms. Vat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia gratia.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 37 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ego sum Deus.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 38 Ita ms. Vien. Alii codices,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut vicissim.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 39 Additum  <HI REND="ITALIC">aut</HI>  ex ms. codice Vien.</P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 40 Ms. Vat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">servientes.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 41 Ita ms. Vien. Alias,  <HI REND="ITALIC">propriae armis opis.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 42 Ms. Reg. et 3 edd.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">calciabit.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 43 Vox  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae</HI>  abest a ms. codice Vaticano.</P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 44 Addita particula  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut</HI>  ex ms. codice Vien.</P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 45 Ms. codex Regius cum editis quatuor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">currendo.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 46 Ms. Reg.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">amicitior . . . inimicitior.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 47 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">detrahat in lege peccati.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 48 Mss. codices Reg., Vatic. et editi Grin. et
Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">zabolus.</HI>  Sacchinus: Desunt quaedam in hanc,
opinor, sententiam:  <HI REND="ITALIC">In promptu est ergo dignoscere
unde victoria sit, ubi Christus cum spiritu, zabulus cum
carne contendunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 49 Ita ms. Reg. et edd. Bad. et Grin. Alii codd.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut
contra.</HI>  Vide praecedentia.</P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 50 Ms. Vien. et ed. Schot.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">reviviscere.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 51 Ms. Vat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Excitabar.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 52 Ms. Vien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quoniam tu.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 53 Ms. Reg. et edd. Bad. et Grav.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et terribilia.</HI></P> <P COM="0429"><COL N="0429"></COL> 54 Sic omnes codices praeter Rosv., in quo  <HI REND="ITALIC">enarrant.</HI>  
