ut sinu facto ibi celare aliquid possent. Inquit
supra Paulin.:

 <POEM COM="0543"><L INDENT=1>Vestis in altum</L> <L>Succinctae sinibus clausum mandaverat aurum,</L> <L>Suspendens fluidam nudato poplite vestem.</L></POEM>  

Hoc idem fieri solitum docet Plutarchus in Coriolano,
ubi candidatos olim sine tunicis ad comitia accessisse
ait, ne incluso in eisdem auro suffragia mercarentur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Azwston ejbouvlonto proivenai, kaiú ajcivtwna
toiðû polivtaiû toún deovmenon aujtwðn.</FOREIGN>  
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Discinctum volebant,
ac sine tunica ad cives accedere candidatum.</HI>  Ovid.
Amor. lib. I:

 <POEM COM="0543"><L>Quid puerum Veneris pretio prostare jubetis?</L> <L INDENT=1>Quo pretium condat, non habet ille sinum.</L></POEM>  

Horat. lib. II, sat. 3:

 <POEM COM="0543"><L>Ferre sinu laxo, donare, et ludere vidi.</L></POEM>  

 <COL N="0543D"></COL> Super his consule Oct. Ferrar. de Re vest. MURATORIUS.</NOTE>  fieret custodia furti,</L> <L><HI REND=BOLD>481-482</HI>  Cujus sacrilegam fuerat manus ausa rapinam.</L> <L>Ipse suum sibi ferret onus, solumque gravaret,</L> <L>Pollueretque suae letalis sarcina praedae,</L> <L N=585>Ut nihil ex illo vacuum impietate maneret,</L> <L>Qui spolium sceleris sacris ex aedibus actum</L> <L>Includens habitu cincto substringeret <NOTE N="(b)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">contingeret.</HI>  Noster codex,  <HI REND="ITALIC">substringeret.</HI></NOTE>  ipsum,</L> <L>Atque suis signum praetenderet ipse catenis.</L> <L>Namque brevi captus mutavit cingula vinclis,</L> <L N=590>Utque aurum sinibus discincta veste solutis</L> <L>Decidit, ex ipsa fuerat qua cinctus habena</L> <L>Vinctus eas, quas in sacra dona tetenderat audax</L> <L>Praedo manus, proprii captus nodamine lori</L> <L>Rettulit et praedae vacuas, et reste <NOTE N="(c)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">rete.</HI>  Noster codex,  <HI REND="ITALIC">reste:</HI>  quod magis
placet.</NOTE>  repletas.</L> <L N=595><COL N="0543B"></COL> Verum si penitus totam spectare velimus</L> <L>Ordinis exacti seriem magis ac magis omni</L> <L>In specie, vel qua latuit scelus, atque reclusum <NOTE N="(d)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vel qua latuit, quave arte reclusus.</HI>  Utraque
lectio probabilis.</NOTE>  </L> <L>Claruit, admiranda Dei cernemus operta</L> <L>Felicem gessisse manu. Jam plurima retro</L> <L N=600>Diximus, ut fugiens non fugerit, utque redactis</L> <L>Passibus emensos sua per vestigia cursus</L> <L>In cassum totiens volvente relegerit orso</L> <L>Longinquis exclusus, et ad vicina recussus <NOTE N="(e)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">recursus.</HI>  At nostri codicis lectio mihi
magis arridet.</NOTE> .</L> <L><COL N="0544A"></COL> Nunc aliud Felicis opus, quod dextera Christi</L> <L N=605>Edidit, ut meritum cari monstraret alumni,</L> <L>Commemorabo pari specimen mirabile signo,</L> <L>Quod reus ipse tremens confesso prodidit ausu <NOTE N="(f)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">auso.</HI>  Utraque lectio probabilis.</NOTE> .</L> <L>Ante tamen, quia res ita <NOTE N="(g)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur. cod. pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">haec:</HI>  at nostri codicis
lectio melior.</NOTE>  postulat, ipsius instar</L> <L>Enarrabo crucis, qualem et pictura biformem</L> <L N=610>Fingere <NOTE N="(h)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Mur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pingere.</HI></NOTE>  consuevit, baculo vel stante bicornem,</L> <L>Vel per quinque tribus dispansam cornua virgis.</L> <L>Forma crucis <NOTE N="(i)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0543" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0543D"></COL> Elegantissima est crucis ista descriptio. Hanc
duplici modo effingi dicit. Alius crucem exhibet ejus
ad instar, in qua Christus redemptionem nostram
consummavit; alter vero monogramma, Graecis Latinisque
notum profert. Singula dispiciamus. MURATORIUS.</NOTE>  gemina specie componitur, et nunc</L> <L>Antennae <NOTE N="(j)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0544" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0544B"></COL> Muratorius legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Antemnae.</HI>  In nostro codice ita
scriptum est, ut queas legere  <HI REND="ITALIC">antennae</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">antemnae.</HI>  
At equidem legendum puto  <HI REND="ITALIC">antennae.</HI> —Minutius in
